  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1230 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nA 595 dam ridge remains centered over the Ozarks with return flow\nadvecting Gulf moisture into the Mid-South. Temperatures are\nrunning 1-5 degrees warmer than 24 hours ago as the ridge is\nexpanding across the region. A Heat Advisory is in effect for\nportions of the Mid-South with heat index values up to 109 this\nafternoon. The hottest heat index values will be felt in the\nDelta Region.\n\nA rather stagnant forecast period as the aforementioned ridge\ncontinues to influence the Mid-South. Another Heat Advisory is in\neffect tomorrow from 12 PM - 8 PM for eastern Arkansas, the\nMissouri Bootheel, and portions of north Mississippi and West\nTennessee. Expansion and additional advisories are likely for the\nrest of the week as the synoptic pattern is dominated by the\nridge. A few diurnally driven showers and thunderstorms could be\nembedded in any shortwaves propagating through the region, but\nconfidence is low due to dry air aloft and a weak wind profile.\n\nThe first glimpse of a pattern change appears to be Sunday as\nweak troughing emerges off the coast of Maine. This trough may\nstretch a backdoor cold front and filter in drier air on Sunday\ninto next week which would bring relief from dangerous heat. In\nthe meantime, the hot and humid pattern is here to stay. Practice\nheat safety and check on sensitive groups.\n\nDNM",
